# p5 mcp: a stdio server that exits 3 at start (p5-mcp-fail's profile), its
# screen opened between two of its tries. The tries come at a 1 s backoff
# that doubles (xfx src/mcp/runtime.rs:90), near 1, 3, 7, 15 and 31 s after
# the binary starts. The screen is opened near 9 s and snapped a second
# later: at least 2 s after the try before and 3.5 s before the try after.
# Those margins are repeatedly observed, not guaranteed: the tries run on the
# binary's own clock, and the harness's starts at its first frame
# (receipts/launch-settle, LAUNCH-SETTLE-F). xfx answers the screen's tools
# request from the last try's failure (src/tui/mcp_menu.rs:786-791): `Its
# tools couldn't load`. fx shows `Loading tools…` until its next try. This
# scenario keeps that difference on a snap (LAUNCH-SETTLE), since
# p5-mcp-fail now waits it out.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-fail-profile.json
wait 9
type /mcp
key Enter
until shown MCP servers  2
key Enter
until shown echo boom-stderr >&2; exit 3
wait 1
snap held
# Each side's own row: a run in which fx's try came early enough to answer
# the screen fails here instead of turning the pair identical
# (LAUNCH-SETTLE-F).
fx: expect held Loading tools…
xfx: expect held Its tools couldn't load
key Escape
wait 0.5
key Escape
